<section class="app-window manager-window" id="m3ter-manager" data-window-title="M3TER Manager" data-window-width="1100" data-window-height="740" aria-label="M3TER Manager" hidden>
  <div id="mm-login" class="mm-login">
    <form id="mm-login-form" class="mm-login-card">
      <span class="mm-mark" data-icon="manager"></span><h2>M3TER Manager</h2>
      <p>Sign in to monitor your meters and manage downlinks.</p>
      <label for="mm-username">Username</label><input id="mm-username" name="username" autocomplete="username" maxlength="256" required />
      <label for="mm-password">Password</label><input id="mm-password" name="password" type="password" autocomplete="current-password" maxlength="4096" required />
      <p id="mm-login-error" role="alert" hidden></p>
      <button id="mm-login-submit" type="submit" class="nes-btn is-primary">Sign in</button>
      <small id="mm-login-help">Checking access…</small>
      {{#if managerDemo}}<small>Simulated network · demo login: <strong>demo / demo-manager</strong></small>{{/if}}
    </form>
  </div>
  <div id="mm-workspace" class="mm-app" hidden>
    <header class="mm-header"><div class="mm-brand"><span class="mm-mark" data-icon="meter"></span><div><strong>M3TER Manager</strong><small>Your network, in view.</small></div></div><div class="mm-connection"><span id="mm-mqtt" class="mm-pill">MQTT disconnected</span><small id="mm-feed">Live feed closed</small><button id="mm-logout" class="quiet-button">Sign out</button></div></header>
    <div class="mm-selector"><label class="mm-search"><span data-icon="search"></span><input id="mm-search" type="search" placeholder="Search name or DevEUI" aria-label="Search meters" maxlength="100" /></label><label class="sr-only" for="mm-device">Choose meter</label><select id="mm-device"><option value="">Choose a meter…</option></select><button id="mm-more-devices" class="nes-btn" hidden>More meters</button><button id="mm-refresh" class="quiet-button" aria-label="Refresh meter data" title="Refresh meter data">↻</button></div>
    <nav class="mm-nav" aria-label="M3TER Manager sections"><button data-mm-tab="overview" aria-current="page">Overview</button><button data-mm-tab="live">Live monitoring</button><button data-mm-tab="analytics">Analytics</button><button data-mm-tab="commands">Commands</button><button data-mm-tab="queue">Queue</button><button data-mm-tab="info">Meter information</button></nav>
    <div class="mm-scroll">
      <div id="mm-notice" class="mm-notice" role="status" hidden></div>
      <div id="mm-error" class="mm-notice mm-error" role="alert" hidden></div>
      <div id="mm-empty" class="empty-state"><span data-icon="radio"></span><h2>A clear view of every M3ter.</h2><p>Choose a registered meter to see its readings, activity, and downlink controls.</p></div>
      <div id="mm-selected" hidden>
        <div class="mm-identity"><div><span class="eyebrow">SWITCH CUMULUS · LoRaWAN</span><h2 id="mm-name"></h2><code id="mm-eui"></code></div><span id="mm-activity" class="mm-pill">No uplink observed</span></div>
        <section data-mm-panel="overview">
          <div class="mm-metrics"><article class="mm-metric mm-energy"><span>Energy accumulator</span><strong><span id="mm-energy">—</span> <em>kWh</em></strong><small id="mm-energy-time">Awaiting telemetry</small></article><article class="mm-metric"><span>Reported voltage</span><strong><span id="mm-voltage">—</span> <em>V</em></strong><small id="mm-voltage-note">Transmitted value · phase mode unknown</small></article><article class="mm-metric"><span>Last uplink</span><strong id="mm-age" class="mm-small-number">Never observed</strong><small id="mm-uplink-time">—</small></article><article class="mm-metric"><span>Nonce</span><strong id="mm-nonce">—</strong><small>Unsigned 32-bit counter</small></article></div>
          <div class="mm-section-heading"><div><h3>Reading trends</h3><small>Cumulative energy and reported voltage · selected analytics range</small></div><button class="nes-btn" data-mm-go="analytics">Explore history →</button></div>
          <div class="mm-charts"><article class="mm-chart-card"><h3>Energy <small>kWh · accumulator</small></h3><div id="mm-overview-energy" class="mm-chart"></div></article><article class="mm-chart-card"><h3>Voltage <small>V · transmitted value</small></h3><div id="mm-overview-voltage" class="mm-chart"></div></article></div>
          <div class="mm-note">Relay state: <strong>Unavailable</strong>. This firmware payload does not report relay state. A queued command does not verify a change.</div>
          <div class="mm-section-heading"><div><h3>Ordinary relay control</h3><small>These controls do not reset energy or increment the nonce.</small></div><div class="mm-actions"><button class="nes-btn is-primary" data-mm-command="relay-on">Relay ON</button><button class="nes-btn" data-mm-command="relay-off">Relay OFF</button></div></div>
        </section>
        <section data-mm-panel="live" hidden><div class="mm-section-heading"><div><h3>Live activity</h3><small id="mm-last-message">Waiting for MQTT messages</small></div><span class="mm-pill">Device events + console observations</span></div><p class="mm-note">Meter activity means an uplink was observed. MQTT connectivity alone does not establish that a meter is online.</p><ol id="mm-events" class="mm-timeline"></ol><button id="mm-events-more" class="nes-btn">Older activity</button></section>
        <section data-mm-panel="analytics" hidden>
          <div class="mm-section-heading"><div><h3>Historical readings</h3><small>Original meter readings, preserved in UTC and displayed in local time.</small></div><label>Range <select id="mm-range"><option value="3600000">Last hour</option><option value="21600000">Last 6 hours</option><option value="86400000" selected>Last 24 hours</option><option value="604800000">Last 7 days</option><option value="2592000000">Last 30 days</option><option value="custom">Custom range</option></select></label></div>
          <form id="mm-dates" class="mm-actions" hidden><label>From<input id="mm-from" type="datetime-local" required /></label><label>To<input id="mm-to" type="datetime-local" required /></label><button class="nes-btn">Apply range</button></form>
          <div class="mm-charts"><article class="mm-chart-card"><h3>Energy <small>kWh · accumulator</small></h3><div id="mm-history-energy" class="mm-chart"></div></article><article class="mm-chart-card"><h3>Voltage <small>V · transmitted value</small></h3><div id="mm-history-voltage" class="mm-chart"></div></article></div><p id="mm-summary" class="mm-note"></p>
          <div class="table-scroll"><table class="mm-table"><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Accumulator (kWh)</th><th>Voltage (V)</th><th>Nonce</th><th>FPort</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody id="mm-readings"></tbody></table></div><div class="mm-pagination"><button id="mm-history-prev" class="nes-btn">Previous</button><span id="mm-history-count"></span><button id="mm-history-next" class="nes-btn">Next</button></div>
        </section>
        <section data-mm-panel="commands" hidden><h3>Downlink commands</h3><p class="mm-note">Preview the exact frame before enqueueing. All commands are unconfirmed downlinks. Queue acceptance is not device execution.</p><div id="mm-commands" class="mm-command-grid"></div><h3>Command history</h3><div id="mm-command-history"></div><button id="mm-commands-more" class="nes-btn">Older commands</button></section>
        <section data-mm-panel="queue" hidden><div class="mm-section-heading"><div><h3>Pending downlinks</h3><small>ChirpStack’s queue is separate from command history.</small></div><div class="mm-actions"><button id="mm-queue-refresh" class="nes-btn">Refresh queue</button><button id="mm-queue-clear" class="nes-btn danger">Clear queue</button></div></div><p class="mm-note">Unconfirmed commands may leave the queue without a device acknowledgment. A missing queue item does not prove delivery.</p><div id="mm-queue"></div></section>
        <section data-mm-panel="info" hidden><h3>Meter information</h3><dl id="mm-info" class="mm-info"></dl><div id="mm-location" class="mm-note" hidden></div><h3>Public key</h3><code id="mm-public-key" class="mm-long-code">Unavailable</code><button id="mm-copy-key" class="nes-btn" disabled>Copy public key</button><p id="mm-verification" class="mm-note"></p><p class="mm-note">The signature covers nonce and energy (bytes 0–7). Voltage is not signed. A first-seen public key is not an independently authenticated device identity. Current, power, and individual phase measurements are not available in this payload.</p></section>
      </div>
    </div>
    <dialog id="mm-dialog"><form id="mm-dialog-form"><span class="eyebrow">M3TER Manager</span><h2 id="mm-dialog-title">Command preview</h2><div id="mm-dialog-content"></div><label id="mm-confirm-label" class="mm-confirm" hidden><input id="mm-confirm" type="checkbox" /> I understand and confirm this operation for the meter shown above.</label><div class="dialog-actions"><button type="button" class="nes-btn" id="mm-cancel">Cancel</button><button type="submit" class="nes-btn is-primary" id="mm-submit">Enqueue command</button></div></form></dialog>
  </div>
</section>
